A||N||7||whamel||Tail light problem||||1||
Z||000000||whamel||08-21-2000||01:39 PM||||Okay, first off, I want to say I appreciate all the great answers I have been getting for the questions I have been asking lately!  It's helping greatly in getting my GT roadworthy.  Now I have something that's really stumped me and I was wondering if anybody might have an idea of where to start looking.  Here's the scenario:<BR>After getting the car started up, I noticed the tail lights were on (not the head lights, just the tails) - I turn on the headlights, and the tail lights go off.  No brake lights or turn signals at all no matter what, but those could be because I'm missing one of the sockets and probably have bad bulbs.  Is there a common link in the light switch that would make it 'oppose' like this?  I've been digging through my manuals and stuff today and haven't found anything yet.  I'm sure I'll find it when I rip out the old wiring and sort through it, but I'd like to get 'legal' as quick as possible.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-21-2000||01:55 PM||||Check Fuses and tail light bulbs. Sometimes when a fuse blows the lights and such do weird things in GM cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||08-21-2000||02:13 PM||||  Make sure you've got the correct back-up bulbs for your back up lights and double filament turn/brake bulbs in correctly.  If one of the double filament bulbs is burnt out, then your turn signal on that side of the car won't blink.  If it's not the fuses like Orief said, then start looking at the wiring.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-21-2000||03:58 PM||||I forget where it is but there's a ground for the tail bulbs. If that's broke you'll get odd things happening.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-21-2000||11:03 PM||||The ground THEOGER is referring to is located above the right side rear wheel. You'll need to remove the wheel well to check it out, it can be a real pain to get to. Any history on the car?||||reg||1
Z||000005||whamel||08-22-2000||02:43 PM||||Thanks - I'll take a look at these areas.  I'm sure it's one of those.  I had hoped to find a common split point as to where the front and rear lights separate that might be bad, but I haven't found it yet.  Anybody want to come over for a wiring party at my house?  (haha)  I'd love to get this thing going by Sept 10th so I can take it to the show, but I am not very confident I can work out all the bugs by then.<BR>As far as the history - I just bought it on Friday, lots of swapped parts from the conversion, but it's a very strong engine.  I think this one is going to be my favorite!  It has personality!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||08-23-2000||12:51 AM||||Where are you now? MI or OH?<BR>I'll be passing east to west hopefully on Thursday thru OH. (late afternoon?)<BR>If that is where you are now send a # in OH and I'll call when I get there.||||reg||1
